; Tutorial_2_Install_and_Launch.inix -- installing HomerScribe and the tools it uses, then opening it.

[about]
Title=2 - Install and Launch
Intro=HomerScribe_setup.exe installs HomerScribe and, on its last page, offers the tools it uses: Whisper for transcribing, Ollama and a vision model for describing, and the rest. Then the desktop key opens it.
Setup=HomerScribe_setup.exe is downloaded from the HomerScribe page on GitHub.
Homework=Run the setup a second time. Every box on the last page should now say Update or Reinstall, not Install.

[step]

Say=One want: HomerScribe on this computer, with the tools it needs, in one sitting. Everything it uses runs here; once installed, nothing is uploaded.
Key=
Hear=

[step]

Say=I open the downloaded setup program. Windows asks for administrator rights; I say yes.
Key=Enter
Hear=Setup - HomerScribe dialog
Hear=Welcome to the HomerScribe Setup Wizard

[step]

Say=The ordinary installer: Enter takes Next on each page, and the defaults are right.
Key=Enter
Hear=Select Destination Location
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=I take the defaults to the end, where it copies the program and its documents.
Key=Enter
Hear=Installing
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=The last page is the one that matters. It offers each tool HomerScribe uses, as a box saying what it does and its size, already ticked when it is missing.
Key=Tab
Hear=Install Whisper check box, checked
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=Each box's first word is the machine's state read for you: Install when it is missing, Update when a newer one is out, Reinstall when it is current. Transcribing needs Whisper alone, about half a gigabyte.
Key=Down Arrow
Hear=Install Ollama check box, checked
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=Describing needs more: Ollama, the service that runs the model, and the vision model itself, about five and a half gigabytes, downloaded once.
Key=Down Arrow
Hear=Install qwen2.5vl 7b check box, checked, describes video and pictures, about 5.5 GB
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=The text model, about four point seven gigabytes, is only for removing advertisements. A planned misstep: if you will never do that, clear it. Space clears a box.
Key=Space
Hear=not checked
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=Leave the rest as they are. Enter starts them, one after another, each in a window that says what it is fetching.
Key=Enter
Hear=Finish button
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=When they finish, a results box says what was installed and where. Then the key that opens HomerScribe from anywhere: Alt plus Control plus H.
Key=Alt+Control+H
Hear=HomerScribe dialog
Hear=Source paths: edit, https colon slash slash www dot youtube dot com slash watch question mark v equals 3 f 31 o u f q F S M

[step]

Say=Installed and open, with the sample film ready. If a tool was left out, run the setup again and tick its box; a tool already present costs nothing. What this walk taught. I name the step; the reader gives the answer.
Key=
Hear=

[step]

Say=What a box's first word tells you.
Key=
Hear=Install, Update or Reinstall

[step]

Say=What transcribing needs.
Key=
Hear=Whisper

[step]

Say=The installer's last page reads the machine for you: each tool's box begins with Install, Update or Reinstall, so its state is known before anything is ticked.
Key=Tab
Hear=Install Whisper check box, checked
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=Running the setup a second time is safe; boxes for tools that are current say Reinstall, and leaving them clear costs nothing.
Key=

[step]

Say=The tools are installed once for the whole computer, not inside HomerScribe's folder, so an update of HomerScribe never removes them.
Key=

[step]

Say=Everything runs on this computer once installed; transcribing and describing send nothing away.
Key=

[step]

Say=Your settings live in your own application data, so a reinstall keeps them.
Key=

[step]

Say=The key that opens HomerScribe.
Key=
Hear=Alt plus Control plus H
